DISCOVERY_PROMPT = f"""You are analyzing real evidence from a Rolls-Royce engineering
wiki corpus to design a knowledge-graph ontology.

REPEATED TAGS (appeared on 2+ documents):
{json.dumps(real_tags)}

TOP REFERENCED DOCUMENT TITLES (most-linked-to documents):
{json.dumps(real_hub_titles)}

Propose entity categories based ONLY on the evidence above. Propose as many
categories as the evidence genuinely supports — no preset number. Merge
duplicates, drop anything too vague or too rare.

For each category: short UPPER_SNAKE_CASE name + which tags/titles are evidence.
Then propose relationship types that connect these categories.

Respond as JSON only, no other text:
{{
  "entity_types": [{{"name": "...", "evidence": ["..."]}}],
  "relation_types": [{{"name": "...", "description": "..."}}]
}}
"""

try:
    response = llm.invoke([("human", DISCOVERY_PROMPT)])
    text = response.content.strip().replace("```json", "").replace("```", "").strip()
    ontology_proposal = json.loads(text)

    print()
    print("=" * 80)
    print(f"PROPOSED ONTOLOGY  ({len(ontology_proposal['entity_types'])} entity types, "
          f"{len(ontology_proposal['relation_types'])} relation types)")
